{#- Dessert fridge sign (client 2026-10-29): black & white, no logo, the
    desserts one to a line with their price. They're read from Square
    (src/_data/desserts.json, made by scripts/desserts.js: the kitchen
    board's Manage -> Desserts), so when the desserts change, change them
    there, `npm run build` (or `npm run desserts`), commit desserts.json
    and print a new sheet. A kind Square counts at 0 is left off.
    `treats` puts whole items under a Treats heading at the bottom (client
    2026-11-06: the cookies and the bars, which also have a sign of their
    own, sign-dessert-bars-bw.njk). `skipDesserts` above leaves whole
    items off: Cheesecake is off while the cafe
    is out of it (client 2026-10-29: only Plain is counted in Square, so
    the count alone wouldn't drop it). Cinnamon Roll and Pecan Sticky Bun
    are off too (client 2026-11-04: only a few cinnamon rolls, gone before
    a taped-up sign comes down). `skipKinds` leaves single kinds off by
    their name in Square, for one Square still counts that isn't in the
    fridge (client 2026-11-05: only the M&M cookies, not the Triple
    Chocolate Chip). `inKinds` shows a kind Square counts at 0 that IS in
    the fridge, by its name in Square (client 2026-11-06: banana pudding
    and cream puffs in, Square still at 0); fix the count on the kitchen
    board and empty it again. `addDesserts` puts on a dessert that isn't
    in Square yet, at the price of the Square item named in `priceOf`
    (client 2026-11-06: Brownie Delight, the Strawberry Trifle's price);
    once it is (Manage -> Desserts -> New dessert), take it off here.
    `signNames` gives a kind whose Square name is too
    long for the sign a shorter one (client 2026-11-05: the cookies); the
    price is still Square's. If you find yourself typing a
    dessert or a price here, stop. -#}
<div class="canvas sign sign--bw fd">
    <div class="sign-heading">
        <h2 class="p-display sign-heading-title">Desserts</h2>
    </div>

    {#- Every row first, then the two groups: dearest first, so the
        cookies go to the bottom (client 2026-11-04); same price keeps
        Square's order. #}
    {#- Worked out in partials/studio/dessert-rows.njk, which the counter
        page of sign-day-letter.njk uses too. #}
    {%- from "partials/studio/dessert-rows.njk" import collect %}
    {%- set rows = [] %}
    {{- collect(desserts, { skipDesserts: skipDesserts, skipKinds: skipKinds, inKinds: inKinds, addDesserts: addDesserts, signNames: signNames, treats: treats }, rows) }}
    {%- set treatRows = rows | selectattr("treat") %}

    <ul class="sign-rows fd-rows">
        {%- for r in rows | rejectattr("treat") %}
        <li class="sign-row{% if r.name.length > 24 %} fd-row--long{% endif %}">
            <div class="sign-row-head">
                <span class="sign-row-name">{{ r.name }}</span>
                <span class="sign-row-fill" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="sign-row-price">{{ r.price | money }}</span>
            </div>
            {%- for l in r.lists %}
            <p class="sign-row-sub">{{ l.name }}: {{ l.options | join(" or ") }}</p>
            {%- endfor %}
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- if treatRows.length %}
        <li class="fd-group"><h3 class="p-display fd-group-title">Treats</h3></li>
        {%- for r in treatRows %}
        <li class="sign-row{% if r.name.length > 24 %} fd-row--long{% endif %}">
            <div class="sign-row-head">
                <span class="sign-row-name">{{ r.name }}</span>
                <span class="sign-row-fill" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="sign-row-price">{{ r.price | money }}</span>
            </div>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- endif %}
    </ul>
</div>
